course: dictionary
lesson: 2340
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Crush is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means.
explain: «The crushed cane stems left over are burned to power the sugar mills.» Here crush means pressed so hard that the stems are broken up. The word «crushed» is about the shape of the stems, not a feeling.
explain: «At a sleepover Lily tells Maddie she has a crush on Kieran.» Now crush means a strong, often secret liking for someone. The words «has a crush on» and the sleepover clue tell you this is about feelings, not pressing.
explain: Always try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one. Ask yourself: is this about squeezing, feelings, a crowd, or winning?
fact: Crush can be a verb (crush, crushes, crushed, crushing) or a noun (a crush, crushes).
fact: «Crush» means to press something so hard that it breaks, bends or loses its shape.
fact: «Crush» can also mean to defeat completely, as in «a crushing defeat».
fact: A crush is a strong, often secret liking for someone, and a crowd of people pressed tightly together can also be called a crush.
fact: «A jay's feather is blue because of shape: crush it and the blue is gone, leaving grey-brown.»
exercise: «The crushed cane stems left over are burned to power the sugar mills.» What does crushed mean here? | A crowd pushed together | *Pressed so hard that the shape is broken up | Defeated completely | A strong liking for someone
exercise: «At a sleepover Lily tells Maddie she has a crush on Kieran.» What does crush mean here? | A heavy weight pressing down | A crowd of people | *A strong, often secret liking for someone | To win a game easily
exercise: «Their team suffered a crushing defeat.» What does crushing mean here? | A small, friendly game | *A total, overwhelming loss | A crowd cheering loudly | A soft pillow
test: «The pressure does not crush them» is about snailfish in «Snailfish have soft bones and watery bodies, so the pressure does not crush them.» What does crush mean here? | Have a secret liking | *Press so hard that it breaks or loses its shape | Feel very sad | Push a crowd back
test: «A crowd squeezing too tightly can crush people.» In this sentence, crush means? | Defeat people in a game | Make people laugh | A strong secret liking for people | *Press people so hard that they get hurt
exam: In which sentence is crush a noun (a naming word for a feeling or a crowd)? | Their team faced a crushing defeat. | *At a sleepover Lily says she has a crush on Kieran. | Crush the garlic with the back of a knife. | The cans were crushed to save space.
